  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: DiscS&E 3
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: 'A research team is testing several chemical compounds in the lab for
    future cancer studies. One researcher noticed that some of the chemicals being
    tested can irritate the skin or eyes.


    <b>What is the role of the Health
    & Safety Office in this situation?</b>'
  explanation: "The Health & Safety Office\u2014part of the Environmental Health
    & Safety (EHS) team\u2014helps protect researchers by identifying risks, providing
    safety training, and recommending protective equipment and procedures. Their
    role is to prevent injuries and keep the lab environment safe, not to make scientific
    or medical decisions. Their oversight allows researchers to work safely as they
    investigate which compounds might eventually become useful cancer treatments."
  correctAnswer: To provide safety guidance, training, and procedures to reduce risk
    of injury.
  incorrectAnswer1: To decide which chemical compounds should be tested in early
    drug discovery.
  incorrectAnswer2: "To review and approve the research team\u2019s scientific goals
    and study design."
  incorrectAnswer3: To test the chemical compounds to see if they are safe for patients.
  questionRole: Safety & Ethics
  questionType: MultipleChoice
  questionStage: Discovery
